  <!--
    Release_WASM is the browser build. The flag was already used below to keep
    Resources\Graphics3D\** out of it; here it also strips the 3D code itself along with
    its dependencies.

    Why: the 3D pages are already hidden on the web (Products.cs, showInWeb: false), yet
    the browser still downloaded the assemblies. Measured by diffing the published
    assembly lists - 2.6 MB goes away:

      Eremex.Avalonia.Controls3D          1697 KB
      Silk.NET.Vulkan plus two extensions  791 KB
      Silk.NET.Core                         32 KB
      AssimpNetter                          68 KB
      SharpDX.Direct3D11                    14 KB

    DirectX and Vulkan mean nothing in a browser.

    What stays and why: SharpDX.Direct2D1 and SharpDX.DXGI come from Eremex.Drawing.Skia,
    and ReactiveUI is used by the demo itself, outside of 3D.

    PDF cannot be dropped the same way: Eremex.DocumentProcessing arrives transitively
    through Eremex.Avalonia.Controls and does not depend on the demo.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release_WASM'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);DEMO_WEB</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release_WASM'" Label="3D does not reach the browser">
